Machine Room
This is a large room which seems to be air-conditioned. In one corner there is a machine (?) which is shaped somewhat like a clothes dryer. On the 'panel' there is a switch which is labelled in a dialect of Swahili. Fortunately, I know this dialect, and the label translates to START. The switch does not appear to be manipulable by any human hand (unless the fingers are about 1/16 by 1/4 inch). On the front of the machine is a large lid, which is closed.
>open lid
The lid opens.
>put coal in pdp10
Done.
>close lid
The lid closes.
>turn switch with screwdriver
The machine comes to life (figuratively) with a dazzling display of colored lights and bizarre noises. After a few moments, the excitement abates.
